6: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
7:     """Mark background cells in foreground-bearing columns with teal, then repeat the marked grid as a 2x2 tile.
8: 
9:     Input structure
10:     - The input is a nonempty 2D grid with one dominant background color.
11:     - Exactly one non-background foreground color appears, and it is not teal.
12: 
13:     Rule
14:     - Preserve every original foreground pixel.
15:     - In any column containing at least one foreground pixel, recolor background
16:       cells to teal.
17:     - Repeat the resulting grid twice vertically and twice horizontally.
18: 
19:     Key insight
20:     - The foreground pixels select whole columns of the tile; the output is a
21:       repeated copy of that completed tile, not a nearest-neighbor scale-up.
22:     """
